# Nabad Edit — hidden in code, admin-only like Vibe

Edit **lives on `staging` and `main`** (UI + API) but is **invisible** until launched.

## Hidden by default (safe for TestFlight / main)

| Gate | Default |
|---|---|
| `NABAD_SONG_EDIT_PUBLIC_SHIPPED` in `src/feature-flags.js` | **`false`** — must stay false until explicit Pro launch |
| Phone/simulator bake | `nabadSongEditUi: true` on **staging** env (same as Vibe); `false` on production |
| Who sees UI when hidden | **Admin only** (UI flag + `isAdmin()`) |
| Production API | `NABAD_SONG_EDIT_ENABLED` **off** on nabadai.com |
| Staging API | on by default on Vercel Preview (`NABAD_SONG_EDIT_ENABLED`) |

Before **every push to `main`**: `npm run verify:no-producer-ship` (checks Producer + Vibe + Edit flags).

## Daily workflow

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Normal fixes (simulator) | `git checkout staging` → `npm run sim` |
| Sami's phone — staging (Producer + Vibe + Edit) | `npm run run:ios:staging` |

**Staging phone:** `npm run run:ios:staging` bakes **Producer + Vibe + Edit** UI flags (admin-only at runtime).

## When Sami is ready to launch Edit publicly (Pro)

1. Set `NABAD_SONG_EDIT_PUBLIC_SHIPPED = true` in `src/feature-flags.js`
2. Enable `NABAD_SONG_EDIT_ENABLED=1` on **production** Vercel
3. Ship to main + TestFlight with explicit approval (user must say by name: ship feature Edit)

## Agent rules

- **Do not** remove Edit code from staging/main to "hide" it — use the flag.
- **Do not** set `NABAD_SONG_EDIT_PUBLIC_SHIPPED = true` without explicit user approval.
